; Pins grammar.md §13.4: in an `if` condition a `{` ends the expression and opens the block,
; even when the braces look like a lambda. The `{ x => x.ok }` is the if's block (with `=>` as
; junk) and `{ }` is a lambda expression statement on the same line (K0102). Parenthesize the
; call to pass a trailing lambda in a condition.
(SourceFile
  (FuncDecl func f (ParamList)
    (Block
      (IfExpr if (MemberExpr (NameExpr xs) filter)
        (Block (NameExpr x) (ErrorNode) (MemberExpr (NameExpr x) ok)))
      (LambdaExpr))))
